Description: Wild OS system dialogs
 The prompts the system itself puts up, drawn to the Wild OS design:
 .
  * the permission prompt, a polkit agent in place of KDE's, which dims
    every screen, says plainly what the app wants and whether Wild OS
    vouches for it, and asks for the password;
  * the Ctrl+Alt+Del screen (lock, switch user, sign out, change password,
    Task Manager), which works even when an app or the desktop has frozen;
  * "not responding", in place of KWin's own;
  * low battery with battery saver, restart to finish updating with a
    time of the person's choosing, and the App Bridge's Windows mode
    prompt;
  * "32-bit apps are turned off", in place of a bare "Exec format error"
    when a 32-bit program such as Steam is opened while they are off.
